From: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: meson-mx-sdio: tolerate cmd=NULL in threaded IRQ

The hardirq can wake the thread while the timeout handler already
completed the request and cleared host->cmd. WARN_ON(!cmd) then
spams and races with further requests, contributing to -ETIMEDOUT /
card drops on Meson8b SD slots under load.

Re-check cmd under irq_lock and return quietly if already completed.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/meson-mx-sdio.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-mx-sdio.c b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-mx-sdio.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/meson-mx-sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/meson-mx-sdio.c
@@ -427,10 +427,22 @@ static irqreturn_t meson_mx_mmc_irq(int irq, void *data)
 static irqreturn_t meson_mx_mmc_irq_thread(int irq, void *irq_data)
 {
 	struct meson_mx_mmc_host *host = (void *) irq_data;
-	struct mmc_command *cmd = host->cmd, *next_cmd;
+	struct mmc_command *cmd, *next_cmd;
+	unsigned long flags;
 
-	if (WARN_ON(!cmd))
+	/*
+	 * Timeout may have already finished the request and cleared
+	 * host->cmd while this thread was scheduled. That is a normal
+	 * race on this hardware — do not WARN.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_irqsave(&host->irq_lock, flags);
+	cmd = host->cmd;
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&host->irq_lock, flags);
+	if (!cmd)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
 	timer_delete_sync(&host->cmd_timeout);
 
 	if (cmd->data) {
-- 
